  "releaseNotes": "Direct uniform initialization for owned and caller-buffer trees and multi-channel chunks without dense source allocation; reusable caller-owned serialization buffers; allocation-free packet views; faster retained-packet serialization; persistent typed chunk side channels with disk-backed storage support; and channel-local deferred sparse overflow that preserves untouched encodings. Legacy voxel-only packets remain compatible.",
